Fix, on agent-01-fsc:

1. Find the service account. In services.msc, open the "GitHub Actions Runner (...)" service and check the Log On tab.
2. Log in as that user. Open a terminal as that user, either by signing in as them or with runas /user:DOMAIN\svcuser powershell. Run:
sf org login web --alias fsc-qa --instance-url https://htsw--qa.sandbox.my.salesforce.com
Finish Okta and MFA within about 2 minutes, and keep port 1717 free. A browser must be available in that session.
3. Verify, in that same user's terminal:
sf org list auth
sf org display --target-org fsc-qa
fsc-qa should be listed and display should succeed.
4. Re-run the failed job in the Actions tab.

If it still fails

• The alias is case-sensitive. It must match SF_CLI_ALIAS, which defaults to fsc-qa.
• If you logged in under your own account but the service runs as another user (for example NETWORK SERVICE), either repeat the login as the service user, or change the service's Log On account to your user and restart it.
• You can run sf org list auth through the runner by adding a temporary workflow step to see what it sees. Tell me if you want one.
